    <h2>You get one contact for multiple commodities</h2>
    <p>Most exporters specialise in a single commodity. We don't — Green Plus EXIM ships fresh produce, staples, seafood, feed ingredients and fertilizers under one account relationship. If your sourcing needs shift seasonally, or you want to consolidate suppliers, that's a conversation with the same team rather than a new vendor search.</p>

    <h2>Specifications are agreed before anything ships</h2>
    <p>Grade, size/count, moisture, admixture and packaging are confirmed in writing before production or procurement begins. If a lot doesn't meet the agreed specification, we tell you before it ships, not after it clears customs at your end.</p>

    <h2>Documentation matches your market, not a generic template</h2>
    <p>{{ site.complianceStatement }} Every destination has different requirements — a GCC buyer's paperwork looks different from an EU buyer's. {{ site.complianceChecklistCta }}</p>

    <h2>Dual-coast port access</h2>
    <p>Depending on your product and destination, shipments route through {{ site.ports | join(', ') }}. That flexibility usually means shorter inland transit and more shipping-line options than a single-port supplier can offer.</p>

    <h2>Trial orders are a normal way to start</h2>
    <p>Our default MOQ is {{ site.defaultMoq }}. We'd rather earn a repeat contract by performing on a trial order than push a buyer into a volume commitment before they've seen the product land.</p>

    <h2>We say no to what we can't deliver honestly</h2>
    <p>We don't claim certifications we don't hold, and we don't inflate lead times or specs to win an order. If a product is out of season, restricted for export, or a grade we can't currently source, we'll tell you — and suggest an alternative where one exists.</p>
  </div>
</section>

